Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.06,0:00:05.06,sign_26_1_August_25th__Ste,,0,0,0,,{\fad(483,473)}August 25th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.66,0:02:32.87,Main Top,Officer,0,0,0,,Supplies for the Spearhead Squadron\N in Combat District 1?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.12,0:02:32.63,sign_3576_2_August_15th__Ste,,0,0,0,,{\fad(487,437)}August 15th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.11,0:02:38.31,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Major, what's inside this box?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.31,0:02:40.44,Main,L,0,0,0,,S-Special ammunition.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.25,0:02:43.25,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,What's really in it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.50,0:02:47.04,Main,L,0,0,0,,Special ammunition.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.32,0:02:54.00,Main,Man,0,0,0,,A little more... \NA little more to the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.70,0:02:55.74,Main,Man,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.36,0:02:58.11,sign_4229_10_Revolution_Festi,Man,0,0,0,,Revolution Festival
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.74,0:03:03.22,Main,Officers,0,0,0,,Ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.22,0:03:05.34,Main,Officers,0,0,0,,Want to join in the festivities, Major?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.15,0:03:17.58,Main,L,0,0,0,,Initiate ID confirmation.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.58,0:03:19.37,Main,L,0,0,0,,Major Vladilena Milizé.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.37,0:03:23.55,Main,L,0,0,0,,Eastern Theater Combat District 1, \NDefense Unit 1 Command and Control officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.92,0:03:25.87,Main,L,0,0,0,,Activate Para-RAID.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.27,0:03:30.43,Main,L,0,0,0,,Synchronization target: \NSpearhead Processors.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.10,0:03:44.62,Main,Background,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.94,0:03:46.55,Main,Background,0,0,0,,Look at this!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.30,0:03:53.92,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,If it's that hard, you should just quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.00,0:03:59.01,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,We don't really need you for anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.01,0:04:02.38,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Nothing really changes \Nif we don't have a control officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.69,0:04:04.08,Flashback,L,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Kukumila...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.08,0:04:07.28,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Listening to you trying to keep from losing it, \Nwhen you're not even here,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.28,0:04:08.52,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,is distracting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.34,0:04:12.65,Flashback,L,0,0,0,,They don't bother you and the others?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.01,0:04:14.74,Flashback,L,0,0,0,,Those... voices.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.44,0:04:19.56,Main,Boy,0,0,0,,It hurts!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.22,0:04:24.52,Main,Boy,0,0,0,,Mommy!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.85,0:04:26.68,Main,Mom,0,0,0,,Be more careful!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.68,0:04:28.64,Main,Mom,0,0,0,,Silly child.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.62,0:04:38.29,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Even without Shin, Processors have to listen \Nto dying screams all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.77,0:04:42.67,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,And dying instantly when your Juggernaut explodes \Nis one of the best ways to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.39,0:04:46.90,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,We've all seen our friends get their limbs\N blown off, their faces ripped to shreds,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.90,0:04:50.31,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,their bodies get burned all over, or their \Nstomachs ripped open with guts pouring out,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.19,0:04:56.17,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,screaming in pain as they died.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.52,0:05:01.23,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Compared to that, \Nthe voices of the long dead are nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.78,0:05:08.05,Flashback_Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,Any of us could die at any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.20,0:05:19.92,Main,L,0,0,0,,Good evening, everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.92,0:05:21.95,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,I hear you loud and clear, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.95,0:05:24.51,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,Sorry, it's just us guys here tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.51,0:05:25.88,Main,L,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Shuga?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.37,0:05:29.41,Main,L,0,0,0,,Um, where's Captain Nouzen?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.41,0:05:31.52,Main,L,0,0,0,,Did something happen in the battle today?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.52,0:05:35.01,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,No, he's just sleeping. He says he's tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.01,0:05:36.59,Main,L,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.59,0:05:38.39,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,It happens sometimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.66,0:05:42.86,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,I... We don't know the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.86,0:05:46.23,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,But it's probably exhausting. \NNever getting a break 24 hours a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.23,0:05:48.40,Main,L,0,0,0,,Because of the voices of the Legion?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.76,0:05:51.99,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,It's not something that\N you can do anything about.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.99,0:05:55.52,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,We just get tired sometimes, \Nbeing out here, is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.26,0:05:58.03,Main,L,0,0,0,,He's tired, yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.03,0:06:00.83,Main,L,0,0,0,,but the stress on all of you is increasing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.38,0:06:04.26,Main,L,0,0,0,,With all these casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.81,0:06:05.72,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.13,0:06:10.96,Main,L,0,0,0,,You haven't been given one new member \Nsince I arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.96,0:06:12.67,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'll make it happen faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.67,0:06:16.53,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'll do everything I can \Nto make it a top priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.59,0:06:20.07,Main,L,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Shuga?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.49,0:06:22.70,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,Yeah, that'd be good.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.70,0:06:25.73,Main,L,0,0,0,,This unit is defending our most important base.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.97,0:06:28.64,Main,L,0,0,0,,It has the right to receive reinforcements first.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.90,0:06:33.15,Main,L,0,0,0,,Until then, I'll continue to request reinforcements \Nfrom the surrounding units.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.15,0:06:35.98,Main,L,0,0,0,,So please, hang in there a bit longer!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.65,0:06:37.41,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.72,0:06:39.46,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Thanks, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.33,0:06:41.13,Main,L,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.59,0:06:49.68,Dates,L,0,0,0,,{\fad(483,437)}August 16th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.77,0:06:52.39,Main Top,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,So you decided to overstep yourself and\N complain directly to me, Major Milizé?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.56,0:06:58.39,Main,L,0,0,0,,Sir, I can't wait any longer \Nfor replacements for Spearhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.71,0:07:02.38,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'll do anything to help them,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.62,0:07:06.02,Main,L,0,0,0,,even beg you for aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.96,0:07:10.37,Main,L,0,0,0,,I've gone to every department \Nfor help, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.37,0:07:15.63,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,The resupply and Processor replacement plans \Nfor the Eastern Theater are a settled matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.64,0:07:20.24,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,I've already informed them of your request.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.24,0:07:22.75,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,You probably don't know, \Nas it's still an internal matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.75,0:07:24.16,Main,L,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.16,0:07:25.67,Main,L,0,0,0,,We're finally getting supplies?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.67,0:07:29.32,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,So do your duty as best you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.06,0:07:33.56,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,Are you ready for the\N Revolution Festival party?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.73,0:07:38.61,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,Attend the party in a proper dress.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.61,0:07:42.97,Main,Karlstahl,0,0,0,,Isn't that the real job of a \Ndaughter of the Milizé family?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.33,0:07:46.39,Main,L,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.98,0:07:54.32,Dates,L,0,0,0,,August 25th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.83,0:07:54.33,Main Top,A,0,0,0,,Lena, listen...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.20,0:07:57.78,Main,A,0,0,0,,Why did you think \Nthat dress was a good choice?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.78,0:08:00.54,Main,A,0,0,0,,It's pure black, like a mourning dress.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.81,0:08:02.33,Main,L,0,0,0,,It's wonderful, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.33,0:08:04.72,Main,L,0,0,0,,Thanks to this, nobody's asking me to dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.59,0:08:09.51,Main,A,0,0,0,,I agree this party is stupid and boring.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.51,0:08:12.33,Main,A,0,0,0,,But that doesn't mean looking nice \Nis a bad thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.33,0:08:15.13,Main,L,0,0,0,,Well, I think this looks nice enough for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.13,0:08:16.55,Main,A,0,0,0,,That's not the issue.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.45,0:08:18.39,Main,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.63,0:08:22.52,Main,L,0,0,0,,One of my fiancés is over there—\Nthe one who sent me those fancy new sweets!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.96,0:08:24.23,Main,L,0,0,0,,See you later, Lena!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.23,0:08:32.11,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.33,0:08:36.00,Main,L,0,0,0,,Is something wrong, Captain Nouzen? \NIs it the Legion?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.36,0:08:40.88,Italics,S,0,0,0,,No, you didn't call at the usual time, \Nso I thought I'd check in.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.88,0:08:42.31,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Is everything okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.71,0:08:45.33,Italics,S,0,0,0,,If you're busy, \NI can contact you another day.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.91,0:08:48.19,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.25,0:08:56.11,Main,L,0,0,0,,Sorry, this is the time \Nwhen I always call, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.51,0:08:57.76,Main,L,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.21,0:09:01.46,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I wanted to let you know that\N the special ammunition arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.02,0:09:06.84,Main,L,0,0,0,,It got there safely, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.84,0:09:10.14,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Yes. Thank you for the fireworks.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.14,0:09:11.73,Main,L,0,0,0,,Well, it's the Revolution Festival after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.06,0:09:15.27,Main,L,0,0,0,,You saw them with your brother \Nand parents once, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.54,0:09:18.22,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'm sure the others have similar memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.22,0:09:20.60,Italics,S,0,0,0,,It's a Revolution Festival tradition, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.06,0:09:24.50,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Can you see the fireworks \Nfrom the  Palace Luñè where you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.84,0:09:26.29,Main,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.45,0:09:28.51,Main,L,0,0,0,,I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.51,0:09:31.45,Main,L,0,0,0,,But the sky's too bright.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.19,0:09:36.29,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'm sure the fireworks \Nwhere you're at are beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.80,0:09:40.37,Main,L,0,0,0,,The night is dark, and the air is clean.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.02,0:09:42.66,Main,L,0,0,0,,I wish we could see them—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.92,0:09:49.26,Main,L,0,0,0,,Someday, let's all watch the fireworks \Nin District 1 together.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.26,0:09:50.92,Main,L,0,0,0,,I'm sure you'll laugh.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.85,0:09:54.34,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I don't remember them being that bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.34,0:09:56.13,Main,S,0,0,0,,Then see for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.13,0:09:58.53,Main,S,0,0,0,,When the war's over... \NWhen you leave the army,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.53,0:09:59.84,Main,S,0,0,0,,we can all watch them together.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.08,0:10:05.77,Main,S,0,0,0,,I wish Lieutenant Irma and the others \Ncould've seen them, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.77,0:10:09.52,Main,S,0,0,0,,Sorry, my timing was bad again, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.52,0:10:12.76,Italics,S,0,0,0,,No, this is the first time we've ever been able \Nto give them a proper gun salute.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.07,0:10:15.30,Italics,S,0,0,0,,I'm sure they're pleased.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.60,0:10:17.75,Italics,S,0,0,0,,They never liked the mushy stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.27,0:10:19.68,Main,L,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.03,0:10:24.24,Italics,S,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.24,0:10:26.65,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Anju was finally able to cry, \Njust a bit ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.36,0:10:32.62,Italics,S,0,0,0,,She's the type to keep things\N to herself, so that meant a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.46,0:10:36.61,Main,L,0,0,0,,She won't forget Lieutenant Irma.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.61,0:10:38.31,Italics,S,0,0,0,,None of us will.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.75,0:10:42.38,Italics,S,0,0,0,,You remember my brother, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.82,0:10:45.23,Italics,S,0,0,0,,That made me happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.05,0:10:48.86,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Because I wasn't able to remember him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.35,0:10:51.76,Main,L,0,0,0,,Captain Nouzen...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.69,0:10:59.43,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Will you remember us as well, Major?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.54,0:11:10.72,Main,L,0,0,0,,Of course I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.25,0:11:12.07,Main,L,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.86,0:11:16.07,Main,L,0,0,0,,Before that, I won't let you die.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.40,0:11:21.62,Main,L,0,0,0,,I won't let anyone else die.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.99,0:11:30.50,sign_16472_146_August_25th__Ste,L,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,473)}August 25th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.68,0:11:33.27,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,Hey, Eighty-Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.27,0:11:34.46,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,This one, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.83,0:11:38.25,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,It's a present from your master, supposedly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.25,0:11:42.22,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,As if a pig deserves a present \Nfrom a human...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.61,0:11:45.36,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,How'd you manage \Nto get her to sign off? Beg?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.36,0:11:49.51,Main,Soldier,0,0,0,,We're busy with the festival, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.51,0:11:48.39,sign_16940_152_Special_Ammuniti,Soldier,0,0,0,,Special Ammunition
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.42,0:11:55.39,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,What's up?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.39,0:11:56.32,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,What's up, Shin?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.32,0:11:57.23,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.23,0:11:57.82,Main,,0,0,0,,Fireworks?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.82,0:11:58.77,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,So many...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.77,0:12:01.67,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,From the Major? Wow!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.72,0:12:05.93,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Hey, Anju, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.93,0:12:06.77,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.03,0:12:11.57,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I'm wondering if we can tell her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.97,0:12:15.37,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,She's sending us, like, \Npresents and stuff now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.37,0:12:16.76,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Are you worried about her?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.76,0:12:20.21,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,No! Why would I be worried about her?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.21,0:12:21.63,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,But, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.63,0:12:26.18,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,She wasn't scared of Shin. \NSo I think it'd be okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.18,0:12:27.09,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.18,0:12:31.36,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Shin and Raiden, the others...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.36,0:12:34.33,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,None of them are saying anything about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.14,0:12:39.87,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,If we told her, she'd stop calling.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.87,0:12:42.48,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,And that'd be better for all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.79,0:12:44.11,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.54,0:12:47.76,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,I remember what Kaie said to her...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.38,0:12:52.00,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,She's not a bad person, \Nso she shouldn't get involved with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.36,0:12:56.95,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,I think that's why Shin and Raiden \Ncan't bring themselves to say it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.34,0:13:01.50,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,They think it'd hurt her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.50,0:13:09.47,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Anju, are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.00,0:13:11.02,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,With what?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.47,0:13:16.35,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,You've never taken a shower \Nwith anyone before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.87,0:13:20.36,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,I think it's okay now, honestly.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.36,0:13:23.50,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,It's just the two of us. \NThere's no need to hide it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.48,0:13:31.53,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Daiya... said I had pretty hair \Nwhen we first met.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.24,0:13:35.59,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,He knew I was growing my hair out to hide it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.59,0:13:39.92,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,but he asked if I was growing out my hair \Nbecause it was so pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.45,0:13:44.26,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Daiya's gone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.26,0:13:47.27,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,So I think it's silly to keep worrying about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.09,0:13:52.94,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,What about you? Don't you want to tell her?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.87,0:13:58.65,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.35,0:14:03.49,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I don't think I have the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.85,0:14:28.08,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Even if we die, \Nour Reaper will take us there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.37,0:14:35.23,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,I know he'll take me there, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.71,0:14:39.39,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,But then, what about Shin?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.96,0:14:43.76,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Who will carry his heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.61,0:14:51.12,Dates,Kurena,0,0,0,,{\fad(487,437)}August 27th, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.07,0:14:52.02,Italics Top,L,0,0,0,,Undertaker, report.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.38,0:14:56.66,Main,S,0,0,0,,All personnel are ready to begin the attack \Non the Legion forward base.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.85,0:14:59.28,Main,S,0,0,0,,Don't forget. The base is a decoy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.28,0:15:01.39,Main,S,0,0,0,,Watch for the ambushers \Nin the surrounding area.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.79,0:15:05.79,Main,S,0,0,0,,When we've lured them out of their holes, \Ntwo teams from the Fourth Platoon will attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.67,0:15:30.91,Italics,L,0,0,0,,A-Analysis complete! \NLaunch point is 120 kilometers east-northeast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.91,0:15:34.62,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Estimated speed at launch is... \N4000 meters per second?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.62,0:15:38.50,Italics,L,0,0,0,,It's an ultra-long range artillery cannon. \NOne we've never seen before!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.42,0:15:44.95,Italics,L,0,0,0,,I'm calling off the mission!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.95,0:15:47.68,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Retreat, please! Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.71,0:15:49.64,Main,S,0,0,0,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.45,0:16:09.21,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Seems that we shook off our pursuers.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.21,0:16:13.49,Italics,L,0,0,0,,I-I'll get you more personnel! \NI'll make it happen today!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.49,0:16:14.43,Main,S,0,0,0,,Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.12,0:16:17.37,Italics,L,0,0,0,,This doesn't make any sense!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.60,0:16:20.49,Italics,L,0,0,0,,The General said that they already had a plan \Nto bring in replacements.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.49,0:16:21.73,Main,S,0,0,0,,Major Milizé!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.47,0:16:25.63,Main,S,0,0,0,,Everyone, you're okay with it, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.36,0:16:28.25,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.94,0:16:34.70,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Wh-What?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.24,0:16:37.50,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Major, that's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.50,0:16:40.53,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Nothing you do will change a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.53,0:16:42.82,Italics,S,0,0,0,,Captain Nouzen, what are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.82,0:16:44.00,Main,L,0,0,0,,No replacements are coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.00,0:16:46.09,Main,L,0,0,0,,Not a single one. Ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.58,0:16:49.41,Main,S,0,0,0,,We're going to be wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.77,0:16:52.08,Main,S,0,0,0,,This unit is an execution ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.72,0:17:02.31,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.31,0:17:07.46,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,The "replacements" you were just talking about \Nare the Processors that come after us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.95,0:17:10.26,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,She means, "After we're dead."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.67,0:17:13.59,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,We just got some brand-new Juggernauts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.04,0:17:15.71,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Those are for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.97,0:17:23.91,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,The white pigs don't intend to let a \Nsingle Eighty-Six out of the 86th District.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.91,0:17:29.20,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,They conscript us with that\N "five years and you're out" thing as bait.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.20,0:17:31.66,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Then they get us killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.04,0:17:34.80,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,They really are pigs. It's terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.80,0:17:37.65,Italics,L,0,0,0,,That... That's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.96,0:17:41.17,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,The vast majority of Processors die \Nbefore their term is up.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.17,0:17:44.52,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter what you say\N will happen after their term.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.90,0:17:47.38,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,It's when you've got guys like us,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.38,0:17:51.02,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,who manage to survive for years on a battlefield \Nwhere death is certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.02,0:17:53.52,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,The fact that we survived means we're smart,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.52,0:17:56.08,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,and the other Eighty-Six look up to us as heroes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.46,0:17:59.47,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,They can't have us leading a rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.66,0:18:04.22,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,So anyone like that is sent \Nto the worst of the fighting,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.22,0:18:06.17,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,to die there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.50,0:18:11.42,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,And those who still don't die, end up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.75,0:18:14.48,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Combat District 1, Unit 1, Spearhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.97,0:18:19.33,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,The point of this place is \Nto make the soldiers fight until they die.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.67,0:18:22.10,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,This is the last place we'll serve.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.71,0:18:25.37,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We'll all die here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.88,0:18:29.63,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Only after the last one is dead \Nwill replacements come.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.63,0:18:32.10,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,The next group, \Nawaiting their own executions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.75,0:18:37.18,Italics,L,0,0,0,,So we're not making you fight to protect us, \Nbut just to kill you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.18,0:18:40.17,Italics,L,0,0,0,,That's nothing but slaughter!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.48,0:18:43.55,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Did you all know...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.55,0:18:45.63,Main,Anju,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.63,0:18:47.31,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Since when?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.31,0:18:48.96,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,From the start.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.96,0:18:54.38,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,Nobody who went to war, \Nnot my sister or anybody else, came back.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.38,0:18:57.02,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,And we weren't allowed out of the camps.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.45,0:19:02.70,Main,Kurena,0,0,0,,We all knew from the start \Nthat white pigs don't keep their promises.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.70,0:19:05.80,Italics,L,0,0,0,,If you knew, then why did you fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.80,0:19:10.80,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Why not run... \Nor try to get revenge on the Republic?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.07,0:19:14.04,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Revenge wouldn't even be hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.04,0:19:17.25,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We'd just have to sit back \Nand let the Legion through.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.72,0:19:22.79,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We'd die, of course, \Nbut we could take the white pigs with us.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.42,0:19:25.09,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Then why?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.11,0:19:31.70,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Until I was twelve, an old \NAlba woman in District 9 looked after me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.81,0:19:34.55,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Shin was raised by an Alba priest,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.55,0:19:38.60,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,who refused to give up his land \Nand was sent to the camps.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.91,0:19:42.24,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Theo told you before about his captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.90,0:19:46.13,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Kurena knows the very worst of the Alba.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.41,0:19:50.63,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Of course, we all know how awful \Nthe white pigs can be, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.11,0:19:54.12,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,There are also people like Kaie,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.12,0:19:57.96,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,who were abused by other Eighty-Six \Nbecause of the color of their skin.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.05,0:20:04.23,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Anju, Haruto, and Shin have white pig \Nor imperial blood. They're the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.82,0:20:07.60,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,There are scum like that \Namong the Eighty-Six, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.76,0:20:15.43,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,And there were a lot of proud Eighty-Six \Nwho fought to the very end.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.20,0:20:18.32,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Even if most Alba are scum,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.32,0:20:21.73,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,some of you said there wasn't\N any reason to just let us die.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.73,0:20:25.00,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,And not all Eighty-Six are good.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.99,0:20:32.08,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,And so we all decided which we wanted to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.12,0:20:36.49,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Just because scum treats you like scum,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.49,0:20:38.92,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,doing the same makes you no better.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.22,0:20:43.83,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,If the only two paths are to die \Nfighting the Legion, or to die giving up,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.83,0:20:46.97,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,we'll survive to the last moment \Nand go down fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.24,0:20:49.63,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,That's the reason we fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.63,0:20:50.69,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,That's the source of our pride.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.14,0:20:55.36,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,If that means protecting the white pigs, \Nwell, that's not ideal,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.36,0:20:56.56,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,but it's fine with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.46,0:21:06.70,Italics,L,0,0,0,,Even if you know that at the end, you'll die?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.04,0:21:11.07,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Is there anybody stupid enough to hang themselves \Nbecause they know they'll die tomorrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.56,0:21:13.68,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Even if you know \Nyou're going to the gallows,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.68,0:21:16.57,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,you can choose \Nhow you're going to climb up there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.88,0:21:19.36,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We've made our choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.76,0:21:22.59,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,All we have to do now is survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.66,0:23:14.41,sign_33367_293_Eastern_Theater_,Raiden,0,0,0,,Eastern Theater Combat District 16 Unit 1 "Falkes"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.04,0:23:37.09,Main,L,0,0,0,,"Let's Go."
